{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0DFF", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-ph}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a90a5044cb1f149cdcd17b77716db8b7c7e21cca2043cf243a75f1af3e5c9827", "source_text": "The ph topology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:81bafaa378b083cb55f84bc741ae898c101c1e810a447ba0d4ed7a84802bf18b", "unit_id": "tag:0DFF:title"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DFF", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-sheaf}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6d702f158ad5b578d2d64eca06756d0cc15f23091c9577c3cbb89f34d2167887", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we define the ph topology. This is the topology\ngenerated by <ACCENT_0001>tale coverings and proper surjective morphisms, see\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:24899bb1da6d4e3a9ec6fb5c51e76be144ba62baae54a425f837ee6051b89dd9", "unit_id": "tag:0DFF:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0DFF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$f_i$", "MATH_0008": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0009": "$U$", "MATH_0010": "$\\{U_j \\to U\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{X_i \\times_X U \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-ph-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:083537f2ab1cc141fad92775186a70f2c1db35aacef6a69db1f4e9eb6a897a9d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8e6f6bb7c729b8f52fb92414e8f9a70cc545b990b820c1228204cc2150f11dbf", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme and let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>ph covering of <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a family\nof morphisms <MATH_0005> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0006>\nsuch that <MATH_0007> is locally of finite type and such that for every\n<MATH_0008> with <MATH_0009> affine there exists a standard ph covering\n<MATH_0010> refining the family\n<MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e87b00bf32b55336105d4b7136823aed816ab9298853cf4ed853e0c4153ca54f", "unit_id": "tag:0DFG:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DFF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$i_1, \\ldots, i_m \\in I$", "MATH_0002": "$h_j : U_j \\to X_{i_j}$", "MATH_0003": "$f_{i_j} \\circ h_j = h \\circ g_j$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$X_i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-definition-ph-covering}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3a90680ff9402e0d6c645659792ded7abd490ff9fea5b56da1df5bdba3858455", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:694127d020ba280b6bfd223644427aa36ea13939d947a50c593d4a5a4d9f9233", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn other words, there exists indices <MATH_0001> and\nmorphisms <MATH_0002> such that\n<MATH_0003>. Note that if <MATH_0004> and all <MATH_0005> are\nrepresentable, this is the same as a ph covering of schemes by\nTopologies, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f839fec9aee9606c44b418298b69943df7c4832c32d61f98d37321bcd365ce02", "unit_id": "tag:0DFF:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DFF", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth-syntomic-fppf-ph}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6166649e2916014ee6f307bb9fbe4d4043598acd89d8a96a31d3734e3c1b9127", "source_text": "Any fppf covering is a ph covering, and a fortiori,\nany syntomic, smooth, <ACCENT_0001>tale or Zariski covering is a ph covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d74d97c024df847fb359c96d4dc9a129ff65a6c82f75da743ed8c238193e68e7", "unit_id": "tag:0DFH:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DFF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{X_i \\times_U U \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{T_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0007": "$T_i$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{U_j \\to U\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{T_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth-syntomic-fppf}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-refine-fppf-schemes}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{more-morphisms-lemma-fppf-ph}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bd06ffcac4465d0f364273704c2dbc79f58e95fe113b03282d7e3e08e19067e3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:210243ba7df2f29f5fb6ecc98f230e978feee9099790c5bf2d63b6bad892633c", "source_text": "We will show that an fppf covering is a ph covering, and then the\nrest follows from Lemma <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0001> be an fppf covering of algebraic spaces\nover a base scheme <MATH_0002>. Let <MATH_0003> be an affine scheme and let\n<MATH_0004> be a morphism. We can refine the fppf covering\n<MATH_0005> by an fppf covering\n<MATH_0006> where <MATH_0007> is a scheme\n(Lemma <REF_0002>).\nThen we can find a standard ph covering <MATH_0008>\nrefining <MATH_0009> by\nMore on Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0003>\n(and the definition of ph coverings for schemes).\nThus <MATH_0010> is a ph covering by definition.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7e9a5df918ff22eae9b56ec19c1f845c23e3eefef913a2ca084b641e2693e48a", "unit_id": "tag:0DFH:proof"}
